## Hífem ##


<div class="col75p terminal example">...
&lt;select onchange="
   this.form.<span class=focus>style.fontSize</span> = this.value;">
&lt;option>24pt
&lt;option>36pt
&lt;option>12pt
&lt;/select>
...
</div>
<div class=col25p>

<form style="width: 200px; height: 200px; padding: 20px; font-size: 24pt;" onsubmit="return false;">

<select onchange="this.form.style.fontSize = this.value;">
<option>24pt
<option>36pt
<option>12pt
</select>
<br> Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet

</select>

</form>

</div>

* Nomes de propriedade CSS com palavras separadas por **hífen**
* Exemplos
    * <code class=focus>font-size</code>, <code class=focus>font-color</code>
    * <code class=focus>border-style</code>, <code class=focus>border-width</code>
* Na sintaxe CSS/javaScript convertidos em **lowerCamelCase**
    * <code class=focus>fontSize</code>, <code class=focus>fontColor</code>
    * <code class=focus>borderStyle</code>, <code class=focus>borderWidth</code>